      <span class="eyebrow">Talks</span>
      <h2>Three talks, tailored to your room</h2>
      <p>Every talk is shaped around your audience and your event. These are the starting points.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="talks">
      <article class="talk">
        <div>
          <h3>Your goal is a second meeting</h3>
          <p class="for">For founder events, accelerators, networking nights and business chambers</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>Pitching isn't just Shark Tank. It's every conversation with a customer, investor, partner or new hire. This talk shows people how to be understood, not just impressive.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>The one sentence that makes people ask a question</li>
            <li>A seven-step framework, from hook to pressure test</li>
            <li>The 10-second conversation starter for networking</li>
            <li>The test: could someone explain your idea back to me?</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="talk">
        <div>
          <h3>Communicating under pressure</h3>
          <p class="for">For conferences, leadership events and teams</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>What my years in the police, the last few as a detective, taught me about getting to the point when the stakes are real, and how the way you deliver a message changes the outcome.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Reading the room and the person in front of you</li>
            <li>Asking better questions</li>
            <li>Staying clear when you're nervous</li>
            <li>Cutting the waffle without losing the warmth</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="talk">
        <div>
          <h3>Take the leap</h3>
          <p class="for">For women in business events, conferences and community events</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p>From police officer to snail farmer, founder and speaker. A talk about acting before you feel ready and backing yourself when nobody has handed you permission.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Why "perfect" is the enemy of started</li>
            <li>Moving through fear instead of waiting for it to pass</li>
            <li>How I got my first masterclass: I emailed them myself</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin-top:28px">Formats: keynotes and short talks, panels and fireside chats, and two-hour hands-on pitch masterclasses. In person around Perth and WA, or online.</p>
